# Task 4A – Run Containers on the Default Bridge

Two containers were started on the default bridge network.

## Nginx Container

```bash
docker run -d \
  -v /Users/aaru/volumes-test:/usr/share/nginx/html \
  --name first-cont \
  -p 80:80 \
  nginx
```

## MySQL Container

```bash
docker run -d \
  -p 3306:3306 \
  --name sec-cont \
  -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=ROOT \
  mysql:5.7
```

Both containers were running on Docker's default `bridge` network.

---

## Name-Based Communication

The default bridge network does not provide the same automatic container-name DNS resolution available on a user-defined bridge network.

Therefore, relying on:

```text
sec-cont
```

for automatic DNS resolution is not the same as using a user-defined bridge network.

---

## IP-Based Communication

Containers on the default bridge network receive IP addresses from the bridge subnet:

```text
172.17.0.0/16
```

Container-to-container communication can therefore be performed using the container IP address.

### Important Observation

Hard-coding container IP addresses is not ideal because container IP addresses can change.

This is one of the reasons user-defined networks are preferred for application architectures.

