# Important Concepts Learned

## 1. Container Storage

Without a volume:

```text
Container
    |
    v
Writable Layer
    |
    v
Database Data

Container removed
        ↓
Writable Layer removed
        ↓
Data lost
```

---

## 2. Named Volume

With a named volume:

```text
Container
    |
    v
Named Volume
    |
    v
Database Data
```

The volume survives container removal.

---

## 3. Bind Mount

```text
Host Directory
      |
      v
Container Directory
```

Changes made on the host can immediately be reflected inside the container.

---

## 4. Default Bridge Network

The default bridge network provides container networking, but it does not provide the same automatic container-name DNS behavior as a user-defined bridge network.

---

## 5. Custom Bridge Network

A user-defined bridge network provides container-name based communication:

```text
Container A
     |
     | DNS
     v
Container B
```

This makes application-to-database communication easier and more reliable.

